Round 12, item 3 Part B (audit vision-pipeline-1) — NOT KEPT, saved for the founder.

What it does: an LED niche length that niche_inference estimated from the room
type is no longer billed by default. The three LED rows carry only the metres
read off the drawing; one blank row („LED nišos — suveskite ilgį", kiekis null)
names the rooms where no length was read with the estimate per room, and the
Prielaidos panel offers „LED nišos be perskaityto ilgio: Palikti tuščią /
Priimti įvertinimą" (`_overrides.led_nisu_ivertinimas`). Switch:
niche_inference.LED_ESTIMATE_OPT_IN (True = this behaviour, False = Part A only).

Why it is not in the tree — measured 2026-10-03, €0, `--recompute`, against the
tree with items 1, 2, 3A, 4 applied (which itself equals the baseline):

  totals --gate:  in-sample MAE 9.47 % -> 15.44 %, out-of-sample 7.06 % -> 8.67 %  (GATE FAIL, exit 1)
    objektas_b LED  -18.2 % -> -51.6 %   project MAE 16.63 % -> 27.76 %
    objektas_d LED   -2.5 % -> -46.7 %   project MAE  5.18 % -> 19.92 %
    objektas_h LED   -8.5 % -> -16.5 %   project MAE  6.80 % ->  8.81 %
    objektas_a / objektas_c / objektas_g unchanged (A has no estimate; C's two are
    already dropped by the enumerated-room gate; G's LED is not scored)
  rows --gate:    corpus within-10 % 27.5 % -> 26.5 %, € 32.3 % -> 31.4 %      (GATE FAIL, exit 1)
    objektas_d 40.0 % -> 36.0 %, objektas_h 29.2 % -> 20.8 %

i.e. on the projects in the corpus the estimate is closer to the contractor's
billed length than a blank is. Part A (every row fed by an estimate is never
green and names the rooms and metres) stays in the tree either way.

Apply on top of the round-12 tree: git apply docs/superpowers/patches/2026-10-03-round12-led-optin.patch
Strings in AssumptionsPanel are inline Lithuanian; move them to i18n keys if adopted.

